      "message": "Let a reader watch a repository\n\nSaving keeps a repository in reach; watching hears about it. Anyone\nwho may read a repository can watch it from its page or the API, and\nfrom then on their inbox says when a change lands there and when one\nis drawn for a person's look, after whoever the event addressed on its\nown, so an owner who also watches is told once. Watching is an event\nrather than a preference, so the notices it brings replay from the log\nwith everything else; a watch follows a rename and ends with the\nrepository. Stopping is the same event in reverse.\n\nTask: t-6n83efg0y9hjr9y4zsbbga4adt\nChange-Id: Iwatch0135\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
